{"schema_version":1,"seq":5,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132044_0005","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:20:44-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"ArtifactWritten","status":"planning","payload":{"artifact_key":"plan","path":"/Users/timothy.shee/GitHub/LOCAL_worktrees/new-tech-monorepo/agent-workbench-live/worktrees/agentic-development-task-system-v3-ai/20260527__reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete/agentic-development-task-system-v3__ai/agent-workbench-live/runs/2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete/plan.md","summary":"template staged"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":6,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0006","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-001","text":"`lib.metadata.update()` will not be called from the reconciliation script. The script uses `lib.yaml_io.dumps/loads` directly, mirroring `tools/backfill_completion_refs.py`.","reason":"The existing backfill scripts use the direct approach. Both patterns work; consistency with precedent reduces surprise.","impact":"low","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":7,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0007","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-002","text":"If the follow-on commit on `parent_branch` fails (dirty index, hook rejection, etc.), `cmd_complete` logs a warning and proceeds with worktree removal anyway. The lifecycle still reaches `done`; only master is briefly stale.","reason":"Matches the convenience-artifact-don't-block convention already in use elsewhere in `cmd_complete`. Reconciliation script sweeps the residual.","impact":"low","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":8,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0008","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-003","text":"Merge-commit discovery uses `git log --merges --grep=\"Merge branch 'agent/<slug>'\"`. Exactly-one-match is required; zero or multiple matches \u2192 skip with warning.","reason":"This is git's default merge commit message format and what `repos.merge_no_ff` produces today. Other shapes (rebases, custom commit messages) are out of scope.","impact":"medium \u2014 if the message format ever changes, both the forward fix's follow-on commit AND the discovery helper would need updates.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":9,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0009","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-004","text":"The reconciliation script does NOT auto-commit its file changes. The user inspects the diff after `--write` and commits manually.","reason":"Matches `backfill_completion_refs.py` and `backfill_base_ref_sha.py` precedent. Lets the user pick the commit message and timing.","impact":"low","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":10,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0010","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-005","text":"`metadata.save()` accepts an optional `dest` parameter that lets the caller route the YAML write to a specific path (not just `cfg.runs_path / run_id / \"metadata.yaml\"`).","reason":"Inferred from the line-120 signature reference in the explore subagent's report. If absent, fall back to direct `yaml_io.dumps(data) + master_path.write_text(...)`.","impact":"low \u2014 fallback is a 2-line change.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":11,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0011","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-006","text":"The forward fix in `cmd_complete.py` runs from the workbench root checkout (NOT the worktree). The workbench root is already on `parent_branch` after `_do_merge()` returns (the merge happens in the root, not the worktree, because `repos.merge_no_ff` checks out parent_branch in the root before merging).","reason":"This is how the existing self-modifying merge works \u2014 the merge is performed in the root, not the worktree.","impact":"medium \u2014 if `_do_merge()`'s working-directory semantics are different from this assumption, the forward fix's `git add` + `commit` invocation needs to target the right path. Verify during implementation.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":12,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0012","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-001","decision":"Reconciliation script writes `completion.accepted_by: \"reconciliation\"` (literal string).","rationale":"The script can't know who originally accepted a historical run (the data wasn't recorded on master). \"reconciliation\" is unambiguous in the audit trail and clearly distinguishes script-applied entries from human-applied ones.","alternatives_considered":"(i) Leave `accepted_by: null`; (ii) Use git's `user.email`; (iii) Require `--accepted-by` flag on the script.","why_not_alternatives":"(i) violates the schema's \"completion.required: [accepted_by, completion_ref]\" rule. (ii) attributes script behavior to a person who may not have been the original accept-er. (iii) adds friction for what's a one-shot backfill; the literal string is honest about the provenance.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":13,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0013","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-002","decision":"Forward fix uses a follow-on commit (\"metadata: backfill done status for <run_id>\") on `parent_branch`, NOT an `--amend` of the merge commit.","rationale":"`--amend` rewrites the merge commit's SHA. `completion.completion_ref` already records the original merge SHA; amending it would change history retroactively and break the audit trail.","alternatives_considered":"(i) `git commit --amend`; (ii) Single merge commit that includes the `done` write via the worktree's branch carrying the `done` write before the merge.","why_not_alternatives":"(i) rewrites published history. (ii) would require reordering `_do_merge()`'s commit-then-merge sequence so the `done` write is part of the merged branch \u2014 feasible but invasive (would need to write `done` to the worktree, stage and commit on the worktree branch, then merge). The follow-on commit is a smaller and safer surface.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":14,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0014","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-003","decision":"Reconciliation script writes `completion.completed_at` from the merge commit's committer date (`git log -1 --format=%cI <merge_sha>`), NOT from script execution time.","rationale":"\"Completed at\" should reflect when the merge actually landed, not when the backfill happens to run. The committer date is the closest reliable signal.","alternatives_considered":"(i) Wall-clock at script execution; (ii) Merge commit's author date.","why_not_alternatives":"(i) decouples the timestamp from reality; (ii) author date and committer date are usually identical, but if a merge was constructed via `git merge` (no rebase) the committer date is the more accurate \"when this entered the tree\" timestamp.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":15,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0015","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-004","decision":"Follow-on commit message: `metadata: backfill done status for <run_id>`.","rationale":"Mirrors the workbench's existing convention (`runs: <run_id> (complete)` from `stage_and_commit_run_dir`). Says exactly what changed and why.","alternatives_considered":"(i) \"auto-mark complete <run_id>\"; (ii) \"post-merge metadata sync for <run_id>\".","why_not_alternatives":"(i) and (ii) are less specific about what's actually in the diff (a metadata.yaml status flip). The chosen wording matches the doctor warning's framing (\"non-terminal-but-merged\").","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":16,"event_id":"evt_20260527_132535_0016","run_id":"2026-05-27-reconcile-master-metadata-after-cmd-complete","at":"2026-05-27T13:25:35-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-005","decision":"The merge-commit-discovery helper lives in `lib/runs.py` as a new function `find_merge_commit_for_branch(workbench_root, parent_branch, branch_name) -> Optional[str]`.","rationale":"It's used by both the doctor check and the reconciliation script. `lib/runs.py` already owns the abstraction over `runs/` directories and is where the related `is_self_modifying` and `_walk_worktrees` live.","alternatives_considered":"(i) Put it in `lib/repos.py`; (ii) Duplicate the logic in both call sites.","why_not_alternatives":"(i) `lib/repos.py` is about generic git ops, not run-specific concepts; the helper is run-specific. (ii) duplication risks drift in the disambiguation rules.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
